course: dictionary
lesson: 1036
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives each meaning its own number, so you can pick the right one. Booth is a good example: it can be a small place with walls, or a table in a restaurant.
explain: Look at the words around it. «On the day, the school hall becomes a polling station, and each voter puts a cross on a paper in a little booth, in secret.» Polling station, voter and secret tell you the booth is a small, private place for voting.
explain: Now try another one: «The children bought cakes at the booth on the school fair field.» At a fair, a booth is a small stall where things are sold. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check: does it still make sense? If it does, you have found the right one.
fact: A booth is a small, partly closed place for one person or a small group.
fact: A booth can also be a small stall at a fair or market, where things are sold or shown.
fact: In a restaurant, a booth is a table with high-backed seats around it.
fact: A ticket booth or toll booth is a small room for a special job.
fact: Booth with a capital letter is a name, such as «William Booth», who helped to found the Salvation Army.
exercise: «A voter marks a paper in a private booth.» What does booth mean here? | A stall where cakes are sold at a fair | A table in a restaurant with high seats | A wooden bench in a park | *A small, partly closed place for one person
exercise: «The children sold cakes at the booth on the school fair field.» What does booth mean here? | A party tent for dancing | *A small stall where things are sold | A tall tree on the field | Ticket office for trains
exercise: «The family sat in a booth at the restaurant, on high-backed seats.» What does booth mean here? | A little shop for newspapers | A phone box on the street | A small room for a special job | *A table with high-backed seats around it
test: A toll booth on a motorway is where a driver pays a fee to pass. Which meaning of booth is this? | A stall at a market | A table in a restaurant | *A small room for a special job | A small place for one person to make a phone call
test: «William Booth» starts with a capital letter. Why? | Because capital letters are used for every noun | Because it starts a new paragraph | *Because it is the name of a person | Because it is an action word
exam: Which meaning of booth fits «a cake booth at the summer fair»? | A small, partly closed place for one person | A small room for a special job | A table in a restaurant | *A small stall where cakes are sold
